  "prompt": "Terse adversarial review. Offband MeshCore companion firmware. Feature #428:\npersist the caplog (serial-capture) enabled-flag across reboot + restore the sink\nearly on boot so the boot log is captured. Client flow: ENABLE -> reboot -> capture\nresumes and captures boot forward -> reconnect, STATUS shows enabled -> STOP.\n\nDesign constraints (verified against the tree):\n- NodePrefs is a FLAT offset-tracked binary stream, NO version/length/CRC. New fields\n  MUST be appended at the END of DataStore save/load or they shift every later field and\n  corrupt already-deployed configs. Precedent: radio_fem_rxgain (#298) at offset 137.\n- The capture ring is plain-RAM NON-retained by design (nRF52 #378). Only the FLAG\n  persists; the pre-reboot ring is gone -- capture RESUMES and captures the fresh boot.\n- savePrefs() (no-arg MyMesh wrapper) writes the whole prefs file; used by other setters.\n- meshLogSetLevel(max): capture lines with level <= max. Levels 0(BOOT)..3(PACKET).\n\nReview concretely (cite file:line, rank severity):\n1. Append-only correctness: are caplog_enabled(138)/caplog_level(139) appended LAST and\n   in the SAME order in both savePrefs and loadPrefsInt? Any offset/order mismatch?\n2. Backward-compat: a prefs file written before #428 ends at 138. Do the two trailing\n   file.read() calls short-read to EOF and leave the defaults (OFF/DEBUG) set before\n   loadPrefs? Any partial-read hazard from TWO appended bytes (vs one)?\n3. Restore timing: restore is in MyMesh::begin() right after loadPrefs + sanitize. Is the\n   sink guaranteed initialized (static global) at that point? Is this early enough that\n   subsequent boot logging is captured? Anything that logs BEFORE this point is lost --\n   acceptable?\n4. Persist points: ENABLE persists enabled=1/level, DISABLE persists 0. DOWNLOAD does a\n   transient meshLogSetEnabled(false)/resume WITHOUT persisting -- correct that a reboot\n   mid-download would still auto-resume? ERASE clears the ring without touching the flag\n   -- correct?\n5. Level handling: ENABLE persists the raw client level; restore clamps to [0,3]. Any\n   issue with persisting an unclamped level then clamping on restore?\n6. Anything missed -- flash-wear from savePrefs on every ENABLE/DISABLE, races, a spot\n   that should persist but doesn't, or a default not set before loadPrefs.\nIf sound, say so.\n\n--- DIFF ---\ndiff --git a/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp b/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp\nindex d6e03f4d..6dfca934 100644\n--- a/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp\n+++ b/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp\n@@ -246,6 +246,12 @@ void DataStore::loadPrefsInt(const char *filename, NodePrefs& _prefs, double& no\n     // (LNA ON) intact. A uint8 append is all-or-nothing, so there is no partial-read\n     // hazard. Never insert a new field mid-sequence.\n     file.read((uint8_t *)&_prefs.radio_fem_rxgain, sizeof(_prefs.radio_fem_rxgain));      // 137\n+    // #428: caplog persistence, APPEND-ONLY after radio_fem_rxgain. Files written before\n+    // #428 end at 138, so these short-read to EOF and leave the caller-set defaults\n+    // (caplog OFF, DEBUG). Each is a uint8 all-or-nothing read. Keep these LAST; any new\n+    // field goes after caplog_level. (NodePrefs offset map: ...137 fem, 138 enabled, 139 level.)\n+    file.read((uint8_t *)&_prefs.caplog_enabled, sizeof(_prefs.caplog_enabled));          // 138\n+    file.read((uint8_t *)&_prefs.caplog_level, sizeof(_prefs.caplog_level));              // 139\n \n     file.close();\n   }\n@@ -288,6 +294,10 @@ void DataStore::savePrefs(const NodePrefs& _prefs, double node_lat, double node_\n     file.write((uint8_t *)_prefs.default_scope_key, sizeof(_prefs.default_scope_key));     // 121\n     // #298: APPEND-ONLY, must stay last -- see the matching note in loadPrefsInt().\n     file.write((uint8_t *)&_prefs.radio_fem_rxgain, sizeof(_prefs.radio_fem_rxgain));      // 137\n+    // #428: caplog persistence, APPEND-ONL